## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical, on-device NLP that yields actionable summaries from multilingual consumer reviews, a realistic Instacart/Amazon use case, without network dependency.

## Key Concepts
- On-device multilang NLP under tight size constraints
- Feature extraction via lightweight POS or rules
- Sentiment aggregation and justification
- Privacy-first data labeling and offline evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
function scoreFeature(feature, sentences) {
  let score = 0;
  for (const s of sentences) {
    if (s.toLowerCase().includes(feature)) {
      if (/\b(good|great|excellent|loved)\b/.test(s)) score += 1;
      if (/\b(bad|worst|terrible|hate)\b/.test(s)) score -= 1;
    }
  }
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle negation and language switch within a single sentence?
- How would you validate usefulness of summaries to buyers?

